#!/../bin/madc
// Regression guard for the late-drained free-fn-template forward-prototype fix
// (docs/plans/2026-06-15-late-instantiation-prototype-plan.md, Approach A).
//
// Default-constructing std::set / std::map instantiates the full
// <bits/node_handle.h> _Rb_tree/_Node_handle closure. A method body
// materialized late (_Node_handle_common::release) calls a free-fn-template
// instantiation (std::move -> __ns_std_move__o2) that drains through
// translate_module's pending_funcs loop. Before the fix, that instantiation
// got a DEFINITION but no forward PROTOTYPE, so the earlier-emitted release
// body called it before its declaration and c2mir applied the C K&R
// implicit-int rule (`int()`) -> "invalid type argument of unary *" +
// "conflicting types". The fix records pending_funcs-drained instantiations in
// materialized_funcs so Pass 1.95(a) emits their forward prototypes.
//
// Bare default-construction keeps this off the separate empty-_Rb_tree-dtor
// wall (which only triggers when <iostream> is included): the point of THIS
// guard is that the closure COMPILES (the proto gap is closed) and the program
// runs to exit 0.
#include <set>
using namespace std;

int main()
{
	set<int> s;
	return 0;
}
